Usage: ruralz bundle audit [DIR] [FLAGS]

Security and best-practice findings.

Validates the Bundle as ruralz bundle validate does, then checks the rendered
Bundle for security and best-practice findings: Routes without authentication,
cleartext hops, broad Plugin Capabilities and Plugin pool sizing. Prints one
finding per line, a diagnostic's rule being its code, or with --output json one
JSON array. With --environments and no --env it runs once per Environment of
the file, in file order. Exits 1 when a finding is an error, 0 otherwise.

Arguments:
  DIR  Bundle directory or one-file Bundle (default .)

Flags:
  --env NAME           Render with this Environment's overlay and variables, read from --environments
  --environments FILE  Local Environment resources
  --help               Print this help
  --output text|json   Output format (text or json, default text)
